# Shell scripts mounted into Linux containers MUST have LF endings.
# A CRLF `set -eu` becomes `set -eu\r`, and busybox sh reports it as
# "illegal option -" — an error that names neither the file nor the real cause.
# Found when the RedisInsight seeder failed this way after a Windows-side edit.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Makefile        text eol=lf
*.mk            text eol=lf
Dockerfile*     text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
